---
/**
 * 31 · Set, Compact
 *
 * The set with nothing on it.
 *
 * Shipped Plozz spends its pixels on a bezel, a screen inset, a second inset
 * and a stand, and by 16px all four have collapsed into one blue lump. This
 * keeps only the three things that make a television a television — a case, a
 * well with glass in it, and a stand under the middle — and spends everything
 * saved on making the well read as a well.
 *
 * The case is stepped two pixels then one at each corner, the plainest rhythm
 * that is not a plain rectangle. The stand is a neck out of the case bottom
 * into a plinth, and the case's own keyline breaks where the neck meets it, so
 * the two are one object rather than a television standing on a shelf.
 *
 * One light, upper left, carried the same way through every part: the top edge
 * catches it, left faces are lit, bottom and right faces fall away. The bezel
 * throws two steps of shadow across the top and left of the glass and the
 * bottom and right catch a step of it back off the lip — which is what makes
 * the screen a recess rather than a panel painted on the front.
 *
 * The face is the shared 8-wide one, verbatim, centred on the screen and not
 * on the 32-box, and it lands entirely on the flat core with room on all four
 * sides. Nothing is cleared for it; the field was already flat.
 *
 * Measured: case 26×22, bezel 2 at the sides and 2 at the top,
 * screen 20×16, and a flat core of 17×13 with the face on it —
 * 4 clear pixels to its left, 5 to its right, 2 above and 3 below.
 * 10 tones, one light, upper left.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

